{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102/events","html_url":"https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102","id":6130225979,"node_id":"I_kwDOVYQlo88AAAABbWPTOw","number":102,"title":"jsonl-lint: report the line numbers of malformed rows in a JSONL file","user":{"login":"suredesigntshirts","id":96286454,"node_id":"U_kgDOBb029g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96286454?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts","html_url":"https://github.com/suredesigntshirts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntshirts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-31T02:43:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T03:03:39Z","closed_at":"2026-10-31T03:03:39Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## What\n\nAdd a standalone tool, `packages/jsonl-lint`: a CLI that reads a JSONL file and reports every row that is not valid JSON.\n\n- `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file>` prints one line per bad row, `<file>:<line>: <parse error>`, and exits 1 if any row is bad, 0 if none.\n- Line numbers are 1-based. Blank lines (empty or whitespace only) are skipped, not errors. A file whose last line has no trailing newline still has that line checked.\n- A missing file, or no argument, prints a usage or error message to stderr and exits 2.\n- The checking logic is exported from `packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js` as `lint(text)`, returning `[{ line, error }]`, so other tools can call it without the CLI.\n- The workspace has its own `package.json` (name `jsonl-lint`, `\"type\": \"module\"`, a `test` script running `node --test`), no runtime dependencies, and `node:test` tests covering: a clean file, a bad row in the middle, a torn last row (no closing brace, no newline), blank lines, and the exit codes.\n- A short `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` says what it does and how to run it, and the root README's \"What is here\" lists the tool.\n\n## Why\n\nJSONL journals appended from more than one process (or over a network mount) can end up with a torn or interleaved row, which breaks every reader that parses the file. This tool finds such rows by line number.\n\n## Done when\n\n`npm ci && npm test` at the root is green locally and in this repo's `test` workflow, and the CLI behaves as above.\n\nFiled by the ccp_xstate v2 harness as its first real issue (plan item first-real-issue).","closed_by":{"login":"suredesigntshirts","id":96286454,"node_id":"U_kgDOBb029g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96286454?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suredesigntsh